The mechanism is a **black-hole reply path**: inbound SYN/ICMP packets from users arrive at `web_server_1` (the switch/FRR fabric routes them correctly), but when `web_server_1` tries to send a reply to any off-subnet address, the kernel finds no matching route and silently drops it. The server appears "up" locally (Apache listens, same-subnet pings from `dns_server` succeed) but is unreachable from anything outside `10.200.0.0/24`.

